summary:
We’re hiring in SF and London! Come join this dumpster fire :)
Quoting @pfau
@aidan_mclau Pretty sure the dumpster fire was an analogy for OpenAI itself as an institution, not the products they launch.

Encouraging random exploration is not an exploratory strategy that works in the real world and it took everyone way too long to figure that out.
Quoting @_aidan_clark_
@finbarrtimbers As someone else pointed out, I think these issues are much less important than the fundamental one, which is that they (mostly) don’t require tough exploration, which misled a generation of folks into thinking we were anywhere close to scalable solutions for real problems.

@ren_hongyu killed it
To recap the demo (I'm still sweating), o3-mini wrote it's own ChatGPT UI to talk to *itself* via the OpenAI API, we asked o3-mini to write and execute a script in this UI to evaluate *itself* on GPQA, and the resulting script correctly returned 61%.
📷 https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GfQvhE0aIAAsqG9.jpg

It’s very funny to me that I’m getting followed by all these XAI peeps from this message like all I needed to do was compliment someone there hmmm maybe ily Elon?
